hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"96","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever conceals knowledge, Allah Almighty will bridle him with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"97","The soul is from the command of my Lord, and you have been given only a little knowledge.'"
"98","""I took a walk with the Prophet ﷺ on a farm in Al-Madinah, and when he reclined upon a palm-leaf stalk, a group of Jews were passing by. Some of them said, 'We should question him.' Others said: 'Do not question him for he might tell you something that you do not like.' They said to him: 'O Abul-Qasim, narrated to us about the Ruh.' The Prophet ﷺ stood for some time, he raised his head toward the heavens, and I recognized revelation was coming to him, until the revelation ceased. Then he ﷺ said: ""The Ruh is one of the things, the knowledge of which is only with my Lord. And of knowledge, you have been given only a little (17:85).'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3141)"
"99","""The Quraish said to the Jews: 'Give us something that we can ask this man about.' So he said: 'Ask him about the Ruh.' So they asked him about the Ruh. So Allah Most High, revealed: They ask you concerning the Ruh. Say: The Ruh is one of the things, the knowledge of which is only with my Lord. And of knowledge, you have been given only a little (17:85). They replied: 'We have been given immense knowledge, we were given the Tawrah, and whoever has been given the Tawrah, then he has indeed been given a wealth of knowledge.' So the following was revealed: Say: 'If the sea were ink for the Words of my Lord, surely the sea would be exhausted (before the Words of my Lord would be finished.) (18:109)'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3140)"
"100","Are you not surprised at AbuHurayrah? He came and sat beside my apartment, and began to narrate traditions from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ making me hear them. I was saying supererogatory prayer. He got up (and went away) before I finished my prayer. Had I found him, I would have replied to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not narrate traditions quickly one after another as you narrate quickly. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3655)"
"101","While Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing the booty at Al-Ja'rana, somebody said to him ""Be just (in your distribution)."" The Prophet ﷺ replied, ""Verily I would be miserable if I did not act justly."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3138)"
"102","Abu Tufail, come to us. There has been a difference of opinion between me and my friend about the companion of Moses whom he wanted to meet on the way. Did hear anything from Allah's meesenger ﷺ making a mention of anything? Ubayy said: I heard Messenger of Allah (may Peace be upon him) as saying: As Moses was amongst the group of Bani Isra'il, there came to him a person and he said to him: Do you know anyone having better knowledge than you? Moses said: No. Thereupon Allah revealed to Moses: Of course, there is amongst Our servants Khadir (who has better knowledge) than you. Moses asked the way of meeting him. Allah made the fish a sign and it was said to him: Where you miss the fish return to that (place) and you will soon find him. So Moses moved on as Allah wished him to move on. He then said to his young companion: Bring for us the breakfast. Thereupop that young man said to Moses. when he asked him for the breakfast: Don't you see that as we had reached the Sakhra I forgot the fish and nobody made it forget (in our mind) but the satan that I should remind you of it? Mosed said to that young man: This was what we wanted. So they retraced their steps and met Khadir and the events which followed have been described in His Book except that Yunus (the narrator) said that he followed the traces of fish in the ocean. (Using translation from Muslim 2380f)"
"103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Have you considered the night? First it is, then it is no more. So where does it go? He said: Allah knows best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah does whatever He wills."
"104","I am here."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When trust is lost, then await the Hour."" He asked: ""What does it mean for it to be lost?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When authority is given to those who are not qualified, then await the Hour."
"105",""" O Messenger of Allah! When will the Hour be established?"" So the Propher ﷺ stood to perform Salat and when he was finished his Salat he said: ""Where is the one who asked when the hour will be established?"" The man said: ""It was I, O Mesenger of Allah!"" He said: ""What have you prepared for it?"" He said: ""O Messenger of allah! I have not prepared very much of salat nor fasting for it, but I love Allah and His Messenger."" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""A man shall be with whom ever he loves, and you shall be with whomever you love."" So after the advent of Islam, I did not see that anything brought the Muslims more happiness than that. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2385)"
"106","He who desires to ask anything from me let him ask me about it. By Allah, I shall not move from this place so long as I do not inform you about that which you ask. Anas b. Malik said: People began to shed tears profusely when they heard this from Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it repeatedly: You ask me. Thereupon 'Abdullah b. Hudhafa stood up and said: Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafa, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ said repeatedly: Ask me, and (it was at this juncture that 'Umar knelt down and said): We are well pleased with Allah as our Lord, with Islam as our code of life and with Muhammad as the Messenger (of Allah). Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept quiet so long as 'Umar spoke. Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: (The Doom) is near; by Him, in Whose Hand is the life of Muhammad, there was presented to me the Paradise and Hell in the nook of this enclosure, and I did not see good and evil like that of the present day. Ibn Shihab reported: Ubaidullah b. 'Abdullah b. 'Utba told me that the mother of 'Abdullah b. Hudhafa told 'Abdullah b. Hudhafa: I have never heard of a son more disobedient than you. Do you feel yourself immune from the fact that your mother committed a sin which the women in the pre-Islamic period committed and then you disgrace her in the eyes of the people? 'Abdullah b. Hudhafa said: If my fatherhood were to be attributed to a black slave I would have connected myself with him. (Using translation from Muslim 2359c)"
"107","May Allah have mercy upon him; be reminded me of the verse which I had been made to forget. (Using translation from Muslim 788b)"
"108","The actions that we do, are they created (anew), or are they in a form that has already been decreed? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: They are in a form that has already been decreed. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: Then what is the reason for acting? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Umar! One can only reach that outcome through action. He submitted: O Messenger of Allah! Then we will act with diligence."
"109","I had a younger brother whose nickname was Abu Umair. One day the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to our house, and he asked: ""O Abu Umair! What happened to your bird?"
"110","The Muslim who offends most against the Muslims is he who enquires about something which has not been forbidden to men, and it is declared forbidden because of his enquiry. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4610)"
"111","Abu Hurairah said that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I saw (in my dream) a piece of cloud from which ghee and honey were dropping. I saw the people spreading their hands. Some of them took much and some a little. I also saw a rope hanging from Heaven to Earth. I saw, Messenger of Allah, that you caught hold of it and ascended by it. Then another man caught hold of it and ascended it. Then another man caught hold of it and ascended it. Then another man caught hold of it, but it broke, and then it was joined and he ascended it. AbuBakr said: May my parents be sacrificed for you, if you allow, I shall interpret it. He said: Interpret it. He said: The piece of cloud is the cloud of Islam; the ghee and honey that were dropping from it are the Qur'an, which contains softness and sweetness. Those who received much or little of it are those who learn much or little of the Qur'an. The rope hanging from Heaven to Earth is the truth which you are following. You catch hold of it and then Allah will raise you to Him. Then another man will catch hold of it and ascend it, Then another man will catch hold of it and it will break. But it will be joined and he will ascend it. Tell me. Messenger of Allah, whether I am right or wrong. He said: You are partly right and partly wrong. He said: I adjure you by Allah, you should tell me where I am wrong. The Prophet ﷺ said: Do not take an oath. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4632)"
"112","If anyone summons other to follow right guidance, his reward will be equivalent to that of the people who follow him, without their rewards being diminished in any respect on that account; and if anyone summons others to follow error the sin of which sins being diminished in any respect on that account. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4609)"
"113","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a group of his Companions and they were laughing. Thereupon, he said, ""If you ˹only˺ knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep a lot."" Then Jibrīl came to him and said, ""Allah says to you, 'Why are you putting my servants in despair?'"" He said that he returned back to them then said, ""Attempt moderation ˹in your actions as you˺ rejoice."""""
"114","narrates: ""We used to collect the Qur'an from various fragments in the presence of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"115","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: Once the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, came out while we were present at the Suffah. He said: \""Which one of you would like to go to Bathan or Aqeeq and bring back two camels with high humps and shining color every day, acquiring them without committing any sin or severing ties of kinship?\"" The people said: \""O Messenger of Allah! Each one of us would like that.\"" So the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings b"
"116","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Learn the Qur’an, for it will come as an intercessor for its reciter on the Day o"
"117","The goodness upon which we are now, will there come after it any evil from which we should beware?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Hudhayfah! It is obligatory upon you to adhere to the Book of Allah."" Acquire its knowledge and follow the goodness that is in it for you."
"118","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you are those who learn Qurʿan and teach it.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1318)"
"119","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Acquire knowledge of the Qur'an and safeguard it. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! It slips away from a person's mind faster than a she-camel slips away from its rope."
"120","(The narrator Qutaibah said: This tradition has been narrated by Sa'id b. Abu Sa'id in my collection): The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who does not chant the Qur'an is not one of us. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1469)"
"121","The example of the person who is given the Qur'an and faith is like that of a pear, whose taste is good and whose fragrance is also good. And the example of the person who is given neither the Qur'an nor faith is like the colocynth plant, whose taste is bitter and which has no fragrance."" The example of the person who is given faith but not (knowledge of) the Qur'an is like that of a date, whose taste is good but which has no fragrance. And the example of the person who is given (knowledge of) the Qur'an but not faith is like the sweet basil plant, whose taste is bitter but whose fragrance is good."
"122","The people replied: ""Yes!"" So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this Qur'an is like a rope, one end of which is in the Hand of Allah the Exalted, and the other end is in your hands. Hold firmly to it, and after that you will never go astray nor be destroyed."
"123","I am leaving among you the Book of Allah; it is the rope of Allah. Whoever follows it will remain on guidance, and whoever abandons it will be on the path of misguidance.'"
"124","The Qur'an is such an intercessor whose intercession will be accepted, and such a disputant (i.e., it will argue in the court of Allah for its reciter) whose testimony will be confirmed. Whoever makes it his leader, it will lead him to Paradise, and whoever puts it behind his back, it will drive him to Hell."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Whoever does not have expertise in the science of hadith, this wording of the narration may cause him to fall into the misunderstanding that the Qur'an is created and is a creature, whereas this is not the case. The meaning of these words is: as we have written in our books, the Arabs in their idiom sometimes apply the name of a thing to its cause, just as they apply the name of the cause to the thing itself. So when acting upon the Qur'an leads a person to Paradise, the name of acting upon the Qur'an is applied to its cause, i.e., the Qur'an itself. This does not mean that the Qur'an is created."
"125","""There is to be no envy except for two: A man to whom Allah grants wealth and he spends from it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day. And a man to whom Allah grants (memorization of) the Quran so he stands with it (in prayer) during the hours of the night and the hours of the day."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1936)"
"126","Envy is not justified but in case of two persons only: one who, having been given (knowledge of) the Qur'an by Allah, recites it during the night and during the day (and acts upon it), and the person who, having been given wealth by God, gives it in charity during the night and the day. (Using translation from Muslim 815b)"
"127","What do you think if a man has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate? ʿUthmanؓ Said. He should do wudooʿ as for prayer and wash his private part. And ʿUthman ؓ said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; I asked ‘Ali bin Abi Talib, az-Zubair bin al-ʿ Awwam, Talhah bin ʿUbaidullah and Ubayy bin Kaʿb about that, and they told him to do the same. (Using translation from Aḥmad 448)"
"128","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Every child is born upon the natural disposition, but his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian."
"129","The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Every child is born upon the natural disposition (fitrah)"" means: He is born upon that disposition which Allah the Exalted had ordained on the day when He brought forth the people from the loins of Sayyiduna Adam. The evidence for this is the statement of Allah the Exalted: ""The disposition of Allah upon which He has created mankind, so there is no change in the creation of Allah."" He says: There is no change in this creation for which He has created these people, whether it is for Paradise or for Hell, at the time when He brought them out from the loins of Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him), and He said: These people are for Paradise and these people are for Hell. Have you not considered: Regarding the boy whom Sayyiduna Khidr (peace be upon him) killed, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah created him naturally as a disbeliever."" Even though he was between believing parents, Allah the Exalted gave His servant Sayyiduna Khidr (peace be upon him) knowledge about this, even though He did not give His interlocutor Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) knowledge about it. As we have explained in other places in our books."
"130","There is none born but is created to his true nature (Islam). It is his parents who make him a Jew or a Christian or a Magian quite as beasts produce their young with their limbs perfect. Do you see anything deficient in them? Then he quoted the Qur'an., The nature made by Allah in which He has created men there is no altering of Allah's creation; that is the right religion"" (Rūm 30) (Using translation from Muslim 2658b)"
"131","Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the offspring of the pagans. He said, ""Allah knows what they would have done (were they to live)."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6598)"
"132","narrator named Hasan, quoting from Aswad bin Sari’, who was a poet—he was the first person to begin delivering sermons in this mosque—he relates: Once, the situation arose such that (the polytheists’) minor children had to be killed. When this news reached the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), he said: “Are not the best among you the children of the polytheists? Every child that is born is born upon the natural disposition of Islam, until he begins to speak, then his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian.” Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: The words of the narration: “Every child that is born is born upon the natural disposition of Islam”—this refers to the natural disposition which the people of Islam believe in, about which we have mentioned earlier that when Allah Almighty brought forth His creation (the human race) from the loins of our master Adam (peace be upon him), then a person’s acknowledgment of this natural disposition is a part of Islam, so at the time of belief, the attribution of this natural disposition will be made to Islam by way of proximity."
"133","Every child is born on Islam, but his parents make him a Jew and a Christian, just as a beast is born whole. Do you find some among them (born) maimed? The people asked : Messenger of Allah! What do you think about the one who died while he was young? He replied : Allah knows best what he was going to do. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4714)"
"134","The statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Our Lord is amazed at those people,"" is according to the common usage of people, because when someone is addressed, the words used are those that are commonly understood among people. And in this narration, what is meant by being chained is: Muslims will have captured these people from the lands of the polytheists, they will have been bound in chains, and then brought to the Islamic state, until they accept Islam and enter Paradise. In the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Aswad bin Sari’, may Allah be pleased with him, this is also the meaning of the Prophet’s, peace and blessings be upon him, statement: ""Are not your best people the children of the polytheists?"" By these words, it can also be meant: here the word ""min"" is considered omitted, and the meaning is: ""Are not some among the children of the polytheists among your best people?"
"135","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) found a woman killed during a battle, so he expressed disapproval over it and forbade the killing of women and children during battle."
"136","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was asked about the settlements of the polytheists where attacks are made at night and in those attacks their women and children are killed. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: 'They are from among them.' The narrator says: I also heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: 'The pasture is only the property of Allah and His Messenger.'"
"137","I asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about the children of the polytheists: Should we kill them along with their people? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes! They are part of them."" (The narrator states) Then, on the occasion of the Battle of Hunayn, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing them."
"138","There is happiness for this child who is a bird from amongst the birds of Paradise. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Don't you know that Allah created the Paradise and He created the Hell and He created the dwellers for this (Paradise) and the denizens for this (Hell)? (Using translation from Muslim 2662b)"
"139","I will do so.)"
"140","The Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah! What will happen to these children of ours? So Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""There is no compulsion in religion."" Saeed bin Jubair narrates, whichever child wished, joined those Jews, and whichever wished, entered Islam."
"141","I feared that it would be made obligatory upon you and you would not be able to perform it."" (Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates:) The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to encourage people to perform voluntary prayers in the month of Ramadan, however, he did not give them any formal command regarding this. He used to say to others: ""Whoever, in a state of faith and hoping for reward, performs voluntary prayers in Ramadan, his previous sins will be forgiven."" Then, when the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from this world, this matter remained as it was. Then, during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), this matter remained as it was, and in the early period of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) as well. (That is, after this, people began to perform the Tarawih prayer in congregation.)"
"142","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The pen has been lifted from three people: from the sleeping person until he wakes up, from the minor child until he reaches puberty, and from the insane person until he regains sanity."
"143","Ibn Abbas said: A lunatic woman passed by Ali ibn AbuTalib. He then mentioned the rest of the tradition to the same effect as Uthman mentioned. This version has: Do you not remember that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has said: There are three whose actions are not recorded: a lunatic whose mind is deranged till he is restored to consciousness, a sleeper till he awakes, and a boy till he reaches puberty? (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4401)"
"144","she took her child by his arm and lifted him from her litter at the camel. She said Messenger of Allah (SWAS) can this (child) be credited with having performed Hajj. He replied Yes, and you will have a reward. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1736)"
"145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do you really experience this?"" The people replied, ""Yes!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""This is clear faith."
"146","The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Thoughts come to our minds, and for any one of us, it would be more beloved to him to be turned to ashes than to speak of such a thought."" So the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""This is nothing but faith."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) When a Muslim finds such a thing in his heart or such a thought comes to his mind about which it is not permissible for him to speak, which is a state coming from Allah Almighty, or something similar to it, and then, with true faith, he rejects it from his heart and refrains from being firm upon any of these things, then his rejection of this whisper is a part of faith; rather, it is clear faith. (From the words of the hadith) it is not meant that the coming of such thoughts is a part of faith."
"147","A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Messenger of Allah! one of us has thoughts of such nature that he would rather be reduced to charcoal than speak about them. He said: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great. Praise be to Allah Who has reduced the guile of the devil to evil prompting. Ibn Qudamah said ""reduced his matter"" instead of ""reduced his guile"". Ibn Qudamah said ""reduced his matter"" instead of ""reduced his guile"". (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5112)"
"148","The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Some of us have such thoughts that it is a great matter for him to express them."" So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you people really experience this situation? This is clear faith."
"149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “This is clear faith.”"
"150","I believe in Allah and His messengers."
"151","I replied: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has sent me with this message. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Go back! I did not accept what he said, so he struck my chest, and I felt its pain. I returned, for I had no other choice. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: O Messenger of Allah! Did you send him with such and such a message? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Yes. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: O Messenger of Allah! Upon hearing this good news, (people) will rely on the hope of Paradise. And they will fear (in the footnote it is clarified, here the word is incorrectly transmitted. The actual word is: they will become corrupt). So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said (to Sayyiduna Jabir): Sit down."
"152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To have faith in Allah and to strive in His path."
"153","""A man asked the Prophet 'O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?' He said: 'Jihad in the cause of Allah.' He said: 'Then what?' He said: 'then Hajj Al-Mabrir.''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2624)"
"154","“While we were sitting in the mosque, a man entered riding a camel; he made it kneel in the mosque, then he hobbled it and said to them: ‘Which of you is Muhammad?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining among them, so they said: ‘This fair- skinned man who is reclining.’ The man said to him: ‘O son of ‘Abdul- Muttalib!’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘I am listening to you.’ The man said: O Muhammad! I am asking you and will be stern in asking, so do not bear any ill-feelings towards me.’ He said: ‘Ask whatever you think.’ The man said: ‘I adjure you by your Lord and the Lord of those who came before you, has Allah sent you to all of mankind?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘By Allah, yes.; He said: ‘I adjure you by Allah, has Allah commanded you to pray the five prayers each day and night?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘By Allah, yes.’ He said: ‘I adjure you by Allah, has Allah commanded you to fast this month of each year?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘By Allah, yes.’ He said: ‘I adjure you by Allah, has Allah commanded you to take this charity from our rich and distribute it among our poor?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘By Allah, yes.’ The man said: ‘I believe in what you have brought, and I am the envoy of my people who are behind me. I am Dimam bin Tha’labah, the brother of Banu Sa’d bin Bakr.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1402)"
"155","""We were forbidden in the Quran to ask the Prophet about anything not imperative, so we liked it when a wise man from among the people of the desert came and asked him. A man from among the desert people came and said: 'O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and told us that you say that Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has sent you.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Who created the heavens?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'Who created the Earth?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'Who set up the mountains in it?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'Who created beneficial things in them?' He said: 'Allah.' He said: 'By the One Who created the heavens and the Earth, and set up the mountains therein, and created beneficial things in them, has Allah sent you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger said that we have to offer five prayers each day and night.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'By the One Who sent you, has Allah commanded you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger said that we have to pay Zakah on our wealth.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'By the One Who sent you, has Allah commanded you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger said that we have to fast the month of Ramadan each year.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'By the One Who sent You, has Allah commanded you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger said that we have to perform Hajj, those who can afford it.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'By the One Who sent you, has Allah commanded you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By the One Who sent you with the truth, I will not do more than this or less.' When he left, the Prophet said: 'If he is sincere, he will certainly enter paradise.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2091)"
"156","When Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muʿadh to Yemen, he said (to him), ""YOU are going to people of a (Divine) Book. First of all invite them to worship Allah (alone) and when they come to know Allah, inform them that Allah has enjoined on them, five prayers in every day and night; and if they start offering these prayers, inform them that Allah has enjoined on them, the Zakat. And it is to be taken from the rich amongst them and given to the poor amongst them; and if they obey you in that, take Zakat from them and avoid (don't take) the best property of the people as Zakat."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1458)"
"157","""The delegation of 'Abdul-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and said: 'We are a group of people from (the tribe of) Rabi'ah, and we can only reach you during the sacred month. Tell us something that we can take from you and to which we may call those who are behind us.' He said: 'I command you to do four things and I forbid you from four: Faith in Allah'- and he explained that to them- 'bearing witness that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, establishing Salah, paying Zakah, and giving me one-fifth (the Khumus) of the spoils of war you acquire. And I forbid you from Ad-Dubba', Al-Hantam, Al-Muqayyir, and Al-Muzaffat.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5031)"
"158","A man said to him: ""Why don't you go out and fight?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Islam is built on five (pillars): Testimony that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, establishing Salah, giving Zakah, Hajj, and fasting Ramadan.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5001)"
"159","I will tell you about its signs: When a slave woman gives birth to her master, and when you see barefoot, naked people (become) rulers (these will be among the signs of the Hour). There are five things whose knowledge is only with Allah. (The command of Allah, the Exalted, is): ""Indeed, the knowledge of the Hour is only with Allah."" (Then the whole verse was recited.) Then that man left. The people searched for him but did not find him. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That was Jibreel (Gabriel), who came so that he could teach the people their religion."
"160","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""With Islam."" He asked, ""What is Islam?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""That you humble your heart for Allah Almighty and you turn your face towards Allah Almighty, and you establish the obligatory prayers and you pay the obligatory zakat. These two are brothers, helping each other. Allah Almighty will not accept the repentance of any servant who commits shirk after accepting Islam."
"161","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""A Muslim eats in one intestine (i.e. he is satisfied with a little food) while a Kafir (unbeliever) eats in seven intestines (eats much). (Using translation from Bukhārī 5396)"
"162","A believer drinks In one intestine whereas a non-believer drinks in seven intestines. (Using translation from Muslim 2063)"
"163","I said: O Messenger of Allah! You have given to so-and-so and so-and-so, but you have not given anything to that person, even though he is a believer. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Is he a believer or a Muslim? He said this three times. Zuhri says: We understand this to mean: By Islam is meant verbally reciting the testimony of faith, and by Iman is meant acting upon it."
"164","Al Miqdad bin Al Aswad reported that he said “Apostle of Allaah ﷺ tell me if I meet a man who is a disbeliever and he fights with me and cuts off one hand of mine with the sword and then takes refuge by a tree and says “I embraced Islam for Allah’s sake. Should I kill him, Apostle of Allaah ﷺ after he uttered it (the credo of Islam)? The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ said “Do not kill him”. I said “Apostle of Allaah ﷺ, he cut off my hand. The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ said, Do not kill him. I f you kill him, he will become like you before you kill him and you will become like him before he uttered his credo which he has uttered now. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2644)"
"165","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring her to me. I brought her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Where is Allah? She replied: In the sky. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Who am I? She replied: You are the Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"166","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Faith has seventy-odd branches, the most virtuous of which is La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship except Allah) and the least of which is removing something harmful from the road. And modesty (Al-Haya') is a branch of faith.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5005)"
"167","The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Faith has seventy odd branches and modesty (Al-Haya') is a branch of faith."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5004)"
"168","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: To testify that there is no god but Allah, to establish prayer, to give zakat, to fast in Ramadan, and to perform Hajj to the House of Allah. The man said: You have spoken the truth. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were amazed at him asking the Prophet (peace be upon him) and then confirming his answer. The man said: Tell me, what is Iman (faith)? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, resurrection after death, and to believe in Qadar, its good and its bad, its sweetness and its bitterness. The man said: You have spoken the truth. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were amazed at him asking the Prophet (peace be upon him) and then confirming his answer. The man said: Tell me, what is Ihsan? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then (know that) He sees you. The man said: Tell me, when is the Hour (Day of Judgment)? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: The one being asked knows no more about it than the one asking. The man asked: What are its signs? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: That a slave woman will give birth to her master. That you will see barefoot, naked, destitute shepherds competing in constructing tall buildings. The narrator says: Then the man turned and left. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Three days later, I met the Prophet (peace be upon him), and the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: O Umar! Do you know who that man was? I said: No. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: That was Jibreel (Gabriel), he came to teach you your religion."",""Translation: He entrusts me with speech"",""so we said"","" """"O Abu Abdur-Rahman"","" some people have appeared among us who excessively recite the Quran and seek knowledge. They claim that there is no predestination and that everything is a result of mere chance."""" He said"","" """"If you meet them"","" inform them that I disassociate myself from them and they disassociate themselves from me."""" Ibn Umar swore an oath that if any of them were to spend gold equal to Uhud"","" it would not be accepted from him unless he believed in predestination. Then he said"","" """"Umar ibn Al-Khattab narrated to us that one day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ  was sitting when a man with extremely black hair and exceedingly white clothes came to him and placed his foot on the Prophet's foot and said"","" 'O Muhammad"","" what is Islam?' He said"","" 'To testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah"","" to establish prayer"","" to give Zakah"","" to fast in Ramadan"","" and to perform Hajj if one is able.' He said"","" 'You have spoken the truth.' We were amazed that he asked him and then confirmed the truth of his answers. He said"","" 'Inform me about Iman.' He said"","" 'To believe in Allah"","" His angels"","" His books"","" His messengers"","" the Day of Resurrection"","" and in destiny"","" both its good and its evil.' He said"","" 'You have spoken the truth.' We were amazed that he asked him and then confirmed the truth of his answers. He said"","" 'Inform me about Ihsan.' He said"","" 'To worship Allah as if you see Him"","" for even though you do not see Him"","" He sees you.' He said"","" 'Inform me about the Hour.' He said"","" 'The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.' He said"","" 'Then tell me about its signs.' He said"","" 'The slave girl will give birth to her master"","" and you will see the barefooted"","" naked"","" destitute shepherds competing in constructing tall buildings.' Then he went away. So I stayed there for a long time"","" and then he said"","" 'O Umar"","" do you know who that questioner was?' I said"","" 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said"","" 'That was Jibril (Gabriel). He came to teach you your religion.'"""""""""
"169","I asked: Even if he has committed adultery, even if he has stolen? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Even if he has committed adultery, even if he has stolen."
"170","The mountain of ""Uhud"" came before us. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr! I do not like that I should have gold equal to the mountain of Uhud, and then by the evening, even a single dinar from it remains with me, except that which I have kept for the repayment of a debt. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) continued walking, and I also continued walking with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr! I said: O Messenger of Allah! I am present. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (In terms of wealth and riches in this world) those who have abundance will be the ones with little (reward) on the Day of Resurrection. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr! Stay here until I come to you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went away until he disappeared from sight. Then I heard a voice. I thought of going forward, but then I remembered the command of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) which he had given me, so I remained there until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I heard a voice. At first, I intended to come to you, but then I remembered your command which you had given me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That was Jibreel (peace be upon him) who came to me and informed me that whoever from my Ummah dies in such a state that he does not associate anyone with Allah, then that person will enter Paradise. (Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, says) I said: O Messenger of Allah! Even if he has committed adultery, and even if he has stolen? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Even if he has committed adultery, even if he has stolen. This same narration is also transmitted with another chain from Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"171","narrate that he said: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""Whoever acknowledges the oneness of Allah and denies all those things that are worshipped besides Him, then the wealth and life of that person will be inviolable, and his reckoning will be with Allah."
"172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Which delegation is this, and which tribe are you from? They replied: We belong to the tribe of Rabi’ah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Welcome to this tribe (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words), this delegation for whom there is no disgrace or regret. They said: O Messenger of Allah! We have come to you from a distant region. Between us and you is the tribe of Mudar, who are disbelievers. Therefore, we can only come to you during the sacred months. Please command us with something that we can convey to those behind us, and by which we may enter Paradise. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them with four things and forbade them from four things. He commanded them to have “faith only in Allah the Exalted.” He said: Do you know what it means to have “faith only in Allah the Exalted”? They replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is to testify that there is no god but Allah, and indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. (Further commands are:) To establish prayer, to give zakat, to fast in Ramadan, and that you pay the khums (one-fifth) from the spoils of war. (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says:) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade them from (using) dubba’, hantam, muzaffat, and naqir (for making drinks). Here, the narrator named Shu’bah sometimes narrates the word naqir and sometimes the word maqir. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Memorize these things and inform those behind you about them."",""Note: Some of the mentioned terms may have different interpretations"",""as translating Old Arabic can be challenging due to language evolution and multiple possible meanings."""""
"173","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Islam is that you bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and indeed Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, is the Messenger of Allah; you establish prayer, you pay zakat, you perform Hajj and Umrah, you perform ghusl for major impurity, you complete ablution, and you fast in Ramadan. He asked: If I do this, am I a Muslim? The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Yes. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: O Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon you! What is Iman (faith)? The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: That you believe in Allah, His angels, His books, and His messengers. You believe in Paradise, Hell, and the Scale. You believe in resurrection after death. You believe in destiny, whether good or bad. The man asked: If I do this, am I a believer? The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Yes! He said: You have spoken the truth. He asked: O Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon you! What is Ihsan (excellence)? The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Ihsan is that you worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then He surely sees you. He asked: If I do this, will I be considered a doer of Ihsan? The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Yes! He said: You have spoken the truth. He asked: O Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon you! When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) come? The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Glory be to Allah! The one being asked does not know more about it than the one asking. If you wish, I can tell you about its signs. He said: Okay. So the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When you see the poor, barefoot, and scantily clad people competing in constructing tall buildings and they become kings.” He asked: Who are meant by the barefoot and scantily clad people? The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The ‘Arib (i.e., the lower class Arabs). The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When you see a slave girl giving birth to her mistress, then this will be one of the signs of the Hour. He said: You have spoken the truth. Then he went back. The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Bring that man to me. (The narrator says) We searched for him everywhere but could not find him. The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Do you know who he was? He was Jibreel (Gabriel), peace be upon him, who came to you to teach you your religion, so take from him. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, never before this time did I have difficulty recognizing him, but this time I recognized him only when he went back. Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: The narrator named Sulaiman Taimi is unique in narrating these words: “So take from him.” And also these words: “And that you perform Umrah, and you perform ghusl, and you complete ablution.”"
"174","I have been commanded to fight against them until they acknowledge that there is no deity except Allah. When they testify that there is no deity except Allah, and believe in what I have brought, then they will protect their lives and wealth from me, except for the right of Islam, and their reckoning will be with Allah the Exalted."" In narrating this tradition, the narrator named Darawardi is unique. This has been stated by the Shaykh."
"175","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I have been ordered (by Allah) to fight against the people until they testify that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah and that Muhammad is Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and offer the prayers perfectly and give the obligatory charity, so if they perform that, then they save their lives and property from me except for Islamic laws and then their reckoning (accounts) will be done by Allah."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 25)"
"176","that a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ""What is Īmān (faith)?"" He said, ""If you are happy with your good deeds and are saddened by your bad deeds, then you are a believer."" The man said, “O Messenger of Allah, then what is sin?” He said, ""If something ˹you do˺ troubles you within, then you should abandon it."" (Using translation from Aḥmad 22166)"
"177","The narrator named Ata says: When I heard this hadith from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), I took this narration to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him about it. He asked: Did you yourself hear Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this? Ata says: I said: He is ill. What is the reason that you do not go to visit him? So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Take us to him. When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went there, I also went with him. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) inquired about his illness, then asked him about this hadith. The narrator says: When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) left from there, he was rubbing his palm and saying: Ibn Umm Abd (i.e., Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him) cannot attribute a false statement to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"178","ʿNo one (truly) believes until he believes in four things; until he believes that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah Who sent me with the truth, and until he believes in the resurrection after death, and until he believes in the divine will and decree.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 758)"
"179","None of you is a believer until I am dearer to him than his child, his father, and the whole of mankind. (Using translation from Muslim 44b)"
"180","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the people are safe, and the believer is the one from whom the people's lives and wealth are safe."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4995)"
"181","Faith has over seventy branches, the most excellent of which is the declaration that there is no god but Allah, and the humblest of which is the removal of a bone from the road. And modesty is a branch of faith. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4676)"
"182","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will admit the people of Paradise into Paradise; He will admit whomever He wills by His mercy. And He will admit the people of Hell into Hell, then He will say: 'Take out from Hell the person who has even a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart.' So those people will be taken out of Hell, and they will have become like charcoal. Then they will be thrown into the river of Paradise, and they will sprout forth from it just as a seed sprouts forth from the silt carried by a flood. Have you not seen it? It is yellow and bends this way and that."
"183","The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) They will be thrown into a river of Paradise, so their burnt parts will fall off at the bank of the river and they will become white like 'tharareer'. It will be written on their necks: These are the ones freed by Allah the Exalted, and (in Paradise) their name will be 'Jahannami' (people of Hell). Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: 'Tharareer' is a small type of flower. This has been stated by the Shaykh."
"184","The (permanent) inhabitants of the Fire are those who are doomed to it, and verily they would neither die nor live in it (al-Qur'an, xx. 47; lxxxvii. 13). But the people whom the Fire would afflict (temporarily) on account of their sins, or so said (the narrator)"" on account of their misdeeds,"" He would cause them to die till they would be turned into charcoal. Then they would be granted intercession and would be brought in groups and would be spread on the rivers of Paradise and then it would be said: O inhabitants of Paradise, pour water over them; then they would sprout forth like the sprouting of seed in the silt carried by flood. A man among the people said: (It appears) as if the Messenger of Allah lived in the steppe. (Using translation from Muslim 185a)"
"185","If this verse were revealed in relation to the Jews (i e. ""This day I have perfected your religion for you and have completed My favours for you and have chosen for you al-Islam as religion"") we would have taken the day of rejoicing on which this verse was revealed. Thereupon 'Umar said: I know the day on which it was revealed and the hour when it was revealed and where Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been when it was revealed. It was revealed on the night of Friday and we were in 'Arafat with Messenger of Allah ﷺ at that time. (Using translation from Muslim 3017b)"
"186","“The adulterer, at the time he is committing adultery, is not a believer; (the wine drinker) at the time he is drinking, is not a believer; the thief, at the time he is stealing, is not a believer; the plunderer, at the time he is plundering with the people looking on, is not a believer.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3936)"
"187","Do not turn unbelievers after me ; one of you may strike the neck of the other. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4686)"
"188","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer at al-Hudaibiyyah after rain which has fallen during the night, and when he finished, he turned to the people and said: Do you know what your Lord has said ? They said: Allah and His Apostle know best. He said: This morning there were among mt servants one who believes in me and one who disbelieves. The one who said: ""We have been given rain by Allah's grace and mercy"" is the one who believes in me and disbelieves in the star ; but the one who said: ""We have been given rain by such and such a rain star,"" is the one who disbelieves in me and believes in the star. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3906)"
"189","The Prophet said, ""Call her."" The slave-girl came, and the Prophet asked, ""Who is your Lord?"" She replied, ""Allah, the Exalted."" The Prophet asked, ""Who am I?"" She replied, ""The Messenger of Allah."" The Prophet said, ""Free her."
"190","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Iman (faith) has more than seventy branches, and modesty is a part of iman."
"191","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Faith has seventy-odd branches, the most virtuous of which is La ilaha illallah (there is none worthy of worship except Allah) and the least of which is removing something harmful from the road. And modesty (Al-Haya') is a branch of faith.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5005)"
"192","""The believer does not insult the honor of others, nor curse, nor commit Fahishah, nor is he foul."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1977)"
"193","""There is no forbearance except for the one who stumbled, and there is no wisdom except for the one who has experience."" (Dai'f) (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2033)"
"194","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us. He said: ""He who does not have trustworthiness has no faith, and he who does not keep his promise has no religion (i.e., the one who does not fulfill his promises)."
"195","I also started walking behind him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr! I replied: I am present, may I be sacrificed for you. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (In terms of wealth and riches in this world) those who possess abundance will be (in terms of reward and recompense) the ones with little on the Day of Resurrection, except for the person who spends his wealth like this and like this, to his right and to his left (i.e., spends in every direction). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this three times. Then Mount Uhud came before us. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Abu Dharr! I do not like that the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) should have gold, and then by evening even a single dinar or a single mithqal of gold remains with them.” I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Then a valley came before us. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went down to its lower part. You descended and I sat at its edge. I thought perhaps you had gone to relieve yourself. You were delayed in returning, so I began to have bad thoughts. Then I heard the sound of supplication. (Later, I inquired about this) and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That was Jibreel, who was informing me about my Ummah, that whoever among them testifies that there is no deity except Allah, and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, then that person will enter Paradise. (Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, says) I said: O Messenger of Allah! Even if he has committed adultery, or even if he has stolen? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Even if he has committed adultery, or even if he has stolen.”"
"196","""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: ""The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the Muhajir is the one who forsakes (Hajara) that which Allah has forbidden to him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4996)"
"197","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""In terms of Islam, the best Muslim among the Muslims is the one from whose tongue and hand other Muslims remain safe."
"198","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever comes on the Day of Resurrection free from three things will enter Paradise. (These three things are:) arrogance, dishonesty, and debt."
"199","The second case is: some questions would have been asked to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and he would have given answers to them, so those answers were narrated but the questions were not narrated, so now it is not permissible for anyone to issue a ruling based on that narration, which applies to every situation. In this, neither the concise and the detailed, nor the general and the specific, have been taken into consideration."
"200","The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 'He will enter Paradise,' means that one Paradise is different from another, because there are various types of Paradise. So, whoever makes that declaration—which is the highest branch of faith—but does not reach the stage of action and then passes away, he will enter Paradise. Whoever, after the declaration, also performs deeds, whether few or many, he too will enter Paradise. But this Paradise will be higher than the previous one, because his deeds are more, so his ranks will be higher and his Paradise will be loftier. It is not the case that all Muslims will enter the same Paradise, even though there is disparity and difference among their deeds, because there are various types of Paradise. It is not the case that there is only one Paradise."
"201","“Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 464)"
"202","Allow me some time (so that I may talk with you). Why do you weep? By Allah, if I am asked to bear witness, I would certainly testify for you (that you are a believer). Should I be asked to intercede, I would certainly intercede for you, and if I have the power, I would certainly do good to you, and then observed: By Allah, never did I hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which could have been a source of benefit to you and then not conveyed it to you except this single hadith. That I intend to narrate to you today, since I am going to breathe my last. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: He who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the messenger of Allah, Allah would prohibit the fire of Hell for him. (Using translation from Muslim 29)"
"203","I am the Messenger of Allah, and this returns to a heart that is certain, then that person's forgiveness is granted."" The narrator says: I asked, ""Did you hear this from Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) himself?"" The narrator says, the people present stared at me, but they said: ""Leave him, he has not said anything wrong. Yes! I heard this from Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) told this, and he heard this from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"204","I know of a word—whoever servant recites this word with a sincere heart and dies upon it, Allah Almighty will make the Hellfire forbidden for him."" That word is: ""La ilaha illallah"" (There is no god but Allah)."
"205","his mother Su'da Al-Murriyyah said: ""Umar bin Khattab passed by Talhah, after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had died, and said: 'Why do you look so sad? Are you upset because your cousin has been appointed leader?' He said: 'No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""I know a word which no one says at the time of death but it will be light in his record of deeds, and his body and soul will find comfort in it at the time of death,"" -but I did not ask him about it before he died.' He ('Umar) said: ' I know what it is. It is what he wanted his uncle (Abu Talib) to say, and if he had known anything that would be more effective in saving him, he would have told him to say it.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3795)"
"206","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When a believer bears witness in his grave that there is no deity except Allah, and recognizes that Allah’s Messenger is Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), then this is what is meant by Allah’s statement: ‘Allah will keep firm those who believe, with the firm word, in the life of this world and in the Hereafter.’” , ,"
"207","He who said:"" There is no god but Allah, He is One and there is no associate with Him, that Muhammad is his servant and His messenger, that Christ is servant and the son of His slave-girl and he (Christ) His word which He communicated to Mary and is His Spirit, that Paradise is a fact and Hell is a fact,"" Allah would make him (he who affirms these truths enter Paradise through any one of its eight doors which he would like. (Using translation from Muslim 28a)"
"208","I am Your Messenger, make the meeting with You beloved to him, make Your decree (i.e., death) easy for him, and make the world little for him. And whoever does not believe in You and does not bear witness that I am Your Messenger, do not make the meeting with You beloved to him, do not make Your decree (i.e., his death) easy for him, and increase for him the worries and difficulties of (this) world."
"209","The inmates of Paradise would see the inmates of the apartment over them just as you see the shining planets which remain in the eastern and the western horizon because of the superiority some have over others. They said: Messenger of Allah, would in these abodes of Apostles others besides them not be able to reach? He said: Yes, they will, by Him, in Whose hand is my life, those who believe in God and acknowledge the Truth, will reach them. (Using translation from Muslim 2831b)"
